domain restricts to positive processing times,\nthe paper's standing assumption for Lemma 3, exactly as the concept's statement now says."},"p:Lax496464Proofs.Ram.W3Final.theorem3_width_time_proved":{"href":"../lax-496464/Lax496464Proofs.Ram.W3Final.theorem3_width_time_proved.html","incident":["e:Lax496464Proofs.Ram.W3Final.theorem3_width_time_proved:conclusion:Lax496464.Theorem3.theorem3_width_time:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The endpoint sweep of Section 4 as a word RAM program: read the word, sort the jobs by start\ntime (`O(n log n)`), build the arrays of the sorted instance and the order of the due dates, then\nsweep the `2n` events — the start of a job takes a free slot (or a fresh one, doubling the mask\nrange `MK = 2^next`), the due date frees it — updating a table with one entry for every set of\noccupied slots and every weight up to `W`, by a flat pass of `MK · (W+1)` cells per event. The\nnumber of slots is at most the width `ω`, so every event costs `O(2^ω · (W+1))` and the run is\nwithin `c · (W+1) · 2^ω · (n+1) + c · sortCost`. The domain restricts to positive processing\ntimes, the paper's standing assumption for the sweep.","nodeId":"p:Lax496464Proofs.Ram.W3Final.theorem3_width_time_proved","semanticId":"Lax496464Proofs.Ram.W3Final.theorem3_width_time_proved","tooltipHtml":"The endpoint sweep of Section 4 as a word RAM program: read the word, sort the jobs by start\ntime (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">O(n log n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</